  "definition": "A condition is an abnormal state of the body or mind that leads to discomfort, problems in functioning, or distress for the affected person or for people around them. The term can be used broadly to cover things such as injuries, disabilities, syndromes, symptoms, deviant behaviors, and unusual differences in body structure or function.",
